        "original_id": "c8e26dd9-6b6e-5618-8b81-5e65a5bc1113",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Newark, Nottinghamshire, England, Eye Manor\n- Organizations: UK Parliament, Conservative Party, Labour Party, Standards Committee\n- People: Robert Jenrick, Patrick Mercer, Fiona Jones\n- Roles: Member of Parliament, Independent MP\n- Events: 1997 general election, 2001 general election, 2014 Newark by-election\n\nFacts:\n- Fiona Jones was elected as Member of Parliament for Newark in Labour's landslide victory in the 1997 general election.\n- Patrick Mercer was elected for Newark as a Conservative in the 2001 general election.\n- Robert Jenrick purchased Eye Manor for £1.1 million in 2009.\n- Patrick Mercer resigned the Conservative parliamentary whip in May 2013 following questions about paid advocacy.\n- Patrick Mercer served as an Independent MP for Newark until his resignation at the end of April 2014 after the Standards Committee suspended him for six months for a sustained and pervasive breach of House rules.\n- Robert Jenrick of the Conservative Party won the Newark seat in a by-election on 5 June 2014.\n- Newark is a UK Parliament constituency in Nottinghamshire, England.\n- Newark is currently represented by Robert Jenrick.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
